<title>USA: PP&amp;L Susquehanna 2 nuke resumes full power.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L Susquehanna 2 nuke resumes full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power and Light Co's 1,094 megawatt (MW) Susquehanna 2 nuclear power unit has resumed full power operations, Nuclear Regulatory Commission said in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Berwick, Pa., was reduced last Friday to 75 percent of capacity due to a condenser leak. The unit was operating at 88 percent power on Monday.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, with a generating capacity of 1,090 MW, is operating at 100 percent power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
